  "verbalization": "Dragmacidin E is implicated in the regulation of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through a series of molecular interactions involving the sodium/bile acid cotransporter. This pathway suggests that Dragmacidin E acts as a modulator of the sodium/bile acid cotransporter, which in turn targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The evidence from multiple paths indicates that Dragmacidin E may influence the activity of this enzyme through a common intermediate, the sodium/bile acid cotransporter, which is also targeted by other compounds like Excisusin B and Artemisitene. The final scores from the paths suggest a consistent and plausible mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains partially inferred. The presence of multiple targets in the sodium/bile acid cotransporter pathway supports the idea that Dragmacidin E may exert its effects through a broader, yet interconnected, network of molecular interactions. The integration of these findings highlights the potential for Dragmacidin E to modulate UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 in a context-dependent manner, possibly through the regulation of bile acid transport and subsequent metabolic processes.",
